# Vercel CLI does NOT read .gitignore. It honours this file plus its own built-in defaults
# (node_modules, .git, .next, .vercel, .env*). Anything untracked but not listed here is uploaded
# into the deployment — which is how local working notes and build artifacts end up shipping.
#
# Verified 2026-10-01 with `vercel deploy --dry --json`: without this file the upload set included
# .workbuddy-ai/memory/*.md and tsconfig.tsbuildinfo. Re-run that command after changing this file.

# Local agent working notes (memory logs, snapshots). Never part of a deployment.
.workbuddy-ai

# Incremental TypeScript build cache — regenerated during the build, no reason to ship it.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
